3. U.S. Food and Drug Administration (United States)               source: "FDA"
================================================================================
Producer:  U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA)
Dataset:   FDA "Recalls, Market Withdrawals, & Safety Alerts" RSS feed
           https://www.fda.gov/about-fda/contact-fda/stay-informed/rss-feeds/recalls/rss.xml
           Filtered to food, beverage, dietary supplement and infant formula
           items. Note: this is the fda.gov recalls RSS feed, not the openFDA
           API.
Licence:   Public domain in the United States (works of the U.S. federal
           government, 17 U.S.C. § 105). No licence is required.
Attribution:
           Source: U.S. Food and Drug Administration (not required; given as
           a courtesy). Use of this data does not imply FDA endorsement.
Uncertain: Many FDA recall entries are company announcements that FDA posts
           "as a public service". Text written by the recalling company is
           not a federal government work, so its public-domain status is not
           guaranteed. The FDA content statement is at
           https://www.fda.gov/about-fda/about-website/website-policies

